---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Factory & Supply Chain — Peptide Manufacturing in China" description="How research peptides are synthesized, purified, lyophilized and released in China: process chain, equipment, capacity model and traceability framework." canonical="/factory/">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › Factory</p>
    <h1>Factory &amp; supply chain</h1>
    <p class="lead muted" style="max-width:840px;">"Made in China" is a location, not a quality standard. What determines the product is the process chain behind it — and whether that chain is documented well enough to audit.</p>

    <h2>The process chain</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>What happens</th><th>Why it matters to buyers</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Peptide synthesis</td><td>Solid-phase synthesis (SPPS), resin loading, coupling cycles</td><td>Sequence fidelity and side-reaction control</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cleavage &amp; deprotection</td><td>Cleavage from resin, side-chain deprotection</td><td>Yield and impurity profile</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Purification</td><td>Preparative RP-HPLC fractions</td><td>Purity and batch-to-batch consistency</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lyophilization</td><td>Freeze-drying under controlled cycle</td><td>Cake structure, residual moisture, stability</td></tr>
        <tr><td>QC release</td><td>HPLC, MS, moisture, appearance</td><td>Documented evidence per lot</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fill &amp; pack</td><td>Vial fill, crimp, label, batch coding</td><td>Traceability to the lot you receive</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Capacity model</h2>
    <p>We do not publish a single "tons per year" figure as if it were audited. Capacity depends on peptide length, purification yield and lyophilization cycle time — the last of these is routinely underestimated, because a full cycle runs for days, not hours (see <a href="/knowledge/peptide-lyophilization-explained/">how freeze-drying works</a>). For planning purposes, share your SKU list and target volumes and we will confirm realistic monthly output and lead time per product.</p>

    <h2>Traceability framework</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Batch number assigned at synthesis and carried through purification, lyophilization, fill and packing.</li>
      <li>Analytical results filed against the batch, not against the product name.</li>
      <li>Retention samples kept for the stated shelf life.</li>
      <li>Deviation log for out-of-specification lots; OOS material is not released.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What buyers can audit</h2>
    <p>Qualified buyers can request a documented quality questionnaire, sample COAs from previous lots, and (for larger programs) a video walkthrough of the production and QC areas. We do not stage factory visits as a marketing device; we answer specific process questions with records.</p>

    <div class="ruo" style="margin:28px 0;">{site.ruo}</div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
